# run_until.sh shipped with 39 CRLF line endings and died on `bash run_until.sh`
# with `syntax error near unexpected token $'do\r'`. A .sh with CRLF is not a Linux
# shell script, and the error points at the loop, not at the line endings. Only the
# shell rule is here because only the shell rule is fatal: 57 tracked files carry
# CRLF, and Python and Lua both read it without complaint.
*.sh text eol=lf

# Listed explicitly rather than applied globally, so the two kinds of file in this
# tree that must never be rewritten stay byte-identical: the cartridge, and the
# BizHawk savestates and movies - a .bk2 or .State is load-bearing binary, and a
# blanket `text` rule would eventually corrupt one of them.
*.nes binary
*.bk2 binary
*.State binary
*.png binary
